linuxmuster-fileserver (1:7.4.0-0~edu) lmn74; urgency=low

  * edulution fork. The package keeps its upstream name, so the epoch 1: is
    what makes it win against the same package from deb.linuxmuster.net.
    The package has no linuxmuster dependencies, so nothing else changes.
  * The version carries the suffix ~edu on top of the epoch, so apt policy,
    dpkg -l and the motd show at a glance that this is the edulution build
    and not the upstream package. "~" sorts before the empty string, so
    1:7.4.0-0~edu stays below a hypothetical 1:7.4.0-0 while still
    outranking every upstream 7.x, which carries no epoch at all.
  * The github-release job asks for contents: write. The repository's
    default GITHUB_TOKEN permission is read, so creating the release would
    have failed with a 403 on the first tag. Granting it on the job keeps
    the default untouched for every other workflow.
  * Release workflow publishes to edulution-io/edulution-package-server
    instead of linuxmuster/deb, into the Ubuntu codename resolute.
  * Depend on edulution-archive-keyring, which owns
    /usr/share/keyrings/edulution.gpg, the keyring the sources entry for
    package.edulution.io names. New or rotated signing keys then reach the
    host with a regular upgrade.

 -- Lukas Lukic-Spitznagel <lukas.spitznagel@netzint.de>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

linuxmuster-fileserver (7.4.0-0) lmn74; urgency=low

  * Add support for Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (Resolute Raccoon)
  * Replace the "ntp" dependency, which no longer exists in Ubuntu 26.04,
    with "chrony | ntpsec | systemd-timesyncd"
  * Add explicit dependency on python3
  * Fix SyntaxWarning about invalid escape sequences emitted by Python 3.14
    on every invocation (banner is now a raw string)
  * Switch packaging to debhelper compat level 13
  * Declare source format 3.0 (native)
  * Build releases on the Ubuntu 26.04 runner image
  * Publish to the lmn74 distribution
  * nsswitch.conf template: use "files" instead of the legacy "compat" NSS
    service and drop "mdns4_minimal", whose module is not installed
  * Depend on libnss-systemd, which provides the "systemd" NSS service the
    nsswitch.conf template refers to
  * linuxmuster-fix-acls: return instead of continue outside a loop, and
    print a correct usage line when no school is given
  * Makefile: drop the unused CONFIGFILE variable and the "all" target that
    referred to a non-existent "build" target

 -- Lukas Spitznagel <lukas.spitznagel@netzint.de>  Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200

